# UI Components

When implementing or modifying UI:

1. Use the existing shadcn/ui components first.
2. Before creating a custom component, search the configured shadcn registries:
   - @8starlabs-ui
   - @23rd
   - @1st-pouf
   - @23rd
3. Prefer existing registry components when they match the requested design.
4. Install registry components using the shadcn CLI.
5. Reuse and customize installed components instead of duplicating them.
6. Preserve the existing project's design tokens, spacing, typography and colors.
7. Do not introduce another UI library unless explicitly requested.
8. If several registry components could work, choose the one that best matches the existing design rather than blindly combining styles.